# ---------------------------------------------------------------- BRK-17, BRK-52, BRK OQ11
in_block(BRK, "BRK-17",
         "- Conditions / exceptions: Applies to banks only. Non-bank tariffs read today do not state a similar exemption (open question 11).",
         "- Conditions / exceptions: Applies to banks only. A non-bank TASE member is outside these rules and, if it is an investment marketer, outside the distribution-fee regulations too; no rule read limits its custody fee on makam or money-market units (BRK-52; open question 11 closed 2026-10-26).")

BRK52 = f"""### BRK-52 Non-bank TASE members: no rule limits their custody fee on makam and money-market units
- Rule: The ban on a custody fee for makam and money-market funds is in the Banking (Customer Service) (Fees) Rules and binds banks only (BRK-17). The distribution-fee regulations, which bar any fee on money-market units held under a distribution agreement (reg. 2(ד), MF-26), bind only a "מפיץ", which they define as "מפיץ שאינו משווק השקעות כהגדרתו בחוק הסדרת העיסוק" (reg. 1); a distributor that is an investment marketer receives a distribution fee under the law instead (s.82(א)(2)). The regulators' joint report of June 2026 (the Supervisor of Banks, the Ministry of Finance and the Securities Authority) says that "מרבית החש"בים מחזיקים ברישיון שיווק" (p.13), that most of them have no distribution agreements with fund managers and are outside the distribution-fee regulations (p.11), and that for non-bank members "לא קיימת הסדרה מקבילה ונדרשת חקיקה" (p.3). No rule read limits a non-bank member's custody fee on makam or money-market units; it follows the member's tariff and client agreement (BRK-24).
- Conditions / exceptions: Not binding: the joint report describes the market and recommends; it binds no one. It also describes practice: at non-bank members a handling fee ("עמלת דמי טיפול בפיקדון ני"ע") is usually a fixed shekel amount, often refunded or not charged, and for custody ("דמי משמרת") "קיים פטור גורף עבור לקוחות החש"בים" (p.11); most non-bank members charge buy and sell commissions on units of active and passive funds instead of a distribution fee (p.11, MF-27). Whether a given member collects its printed custody line on these units is that member's own term (four tariffs: BRK-48). Not known: which non-bank members hold no marketing licence, and whether any of them holds a distribution agreement for a money-market fund (then reg. 2(ד) would bar any fee there). The regulators' press release of 24.6.2026 proposes keeping the banks' distribution-fee model for money-market funds and extending it to the whole market later (a recommendation, not in force). The report is read in a copy hosted by funder.co.il; its PDF on boi.org.il was not located. Added 2026-10-26 (open-question hunt); closes open question 11.
- Figures: none.
- Source: [תקנות השקעות משותפות בנאמנות (עמלת הפצה), התשס"ו-2006 (קובץ התקנות 6464)]({DF06_2}), p.2 (gazette p.494), reg. 1, definition "מפיץ" "מפיץ שאינו משווק השקעות כהגדרתו בחוק הסדרת העיסוק" · checked 2026-10-26 · primary; [חוק השקעות משותפות בנאמנות, התשנ"ד-1994 (נוסח משולב, רשות ניירות ערך)]({ISALAW}), p.60, s.82(א)(2) "תשלום עמלת הפצה למפיץ שהוא משווק השקעות כהגדרתו בחוק הסדרת העיסוק" · checked 2026-10-26 · primary; [כללי הבנקאות (שירות ללקוח) (עמלות), התשס"ח-2008, נוסח משולב (בנק ישראל)]({BOI159}), p.17, first schedule part 4(א)(5), note (2) · checked 2026-10-26 · primary; [{JOINT_T}]({JOINT}), p.13, s.4 item 4 "יצויין כי מרבית החש"בים מחזיקים ברישיון שיווק בשל היותם בעלי זיקה מבנית"; p.11, s.3 items 1 and 3; p.10, note 20; p.3 · checked 2026-10-26 · primary (third-party host: funder.co.il); [הודעה משותפת לעיתונות של בנק ישראל, משרד האוצר והרשות לניירות ערך, 24.6.2026: דוח סופי בנושא מודלי תגמול בפעילות הציבור בניירות ערך]({BOIPR}), p.3 · checked 2026-10-26 · primary. BRK-17, MF-26, BRK-24.
- Scope: general
- Dimensions: `fee-custody`, `fee-trade`
- Likely to change: yes. The report recommends legislation on fees at non-bank members.
"""
insert_after_block(BRK, "BRK-17", BRK52)

oq_replace(BRK, 11, "11. ~~**Custody fee on makam and money-market funds at non-bank members.**~~ Closed 2026-10-26 (open-question hunt): no rule limits a non-bank member's custody fee on makam or money-market units: the bank ban binds banks only, and the distribution-fee regulations exclude an investment marketer from \"מפיץ\", which most non-bank members are, with no distribution agreements (regulators' joint report, June 2026, pp.3, 11, 13) (BRK-52, BRK-17, MF-26). The earlier narrowing (2026-10-26 open-questions audit), that reg. 2(ד) binds any TASE member holding a distribution agreement and so may conflict with the custody lines the four non-bank snapshots in `data/fees/` apply to money-market units, is withdrawn: those lines do not conflict with MF-26 unless a member turns out to be a non-marketer holding an agreement for that fund, which is not known for any of them.")

