# ---------------------------------------------------------------- MF-11 (MF OQ4)
in_block(MF, "MF-11", "The number of business days until redemption cash is usable was not found (open question 4).",
         "When redemption cash arrives is set by regulation under s.46(ד) (prices regulations 1994, reg. 15, as amended in 1999): in a fund whose investment policy keeps foreign securities at no more than 10% of net assets, the redemption amount is transferred on \"היום שבו על המפיץ להעביר למסלקה, לפי סעיף 46(ג)(1) לחוק, את ההזמנה או את ההוראה\", and crediting the distributor's and the holder's accounts counts as the transfer (reg. 15(ב)); in a fund whose policy lets foreign securities exceed 10%, on the first trading day after that day. So in a fund of the first kind, cash from a redemption ordered before the designated hour on a pricing day reaches the holder's account that day; an order after the hour counts as given on the next pricing day (s.46(ג), MF-10). A fixed-date (renewable) money-market fund executes orders only on its fixed date (ISA rules 2024, rule 2(ב)). Example (named, not the rule): Bank Mizrahi Tefahot says that for fixed-date money-market funds \"הסליקה הכספית בחשבונך תתבצע ביום העסקים העוקב ליום ביצוע הוראת המסחר\" (its page). The regulation is read in the Wikisource consolidated text (amendments listed to 2018; reg. 15 tagged only for 1999) and in the 1994 and 1999 gazette scans (page images); an amendment after 2018 was not checked in Reshumot. Open question 4 closed 2026-10-26 (open-question hunt).")
in_block(MF, "MF-11", "- Figures: none\n",
         "- Figures: 10% of net assets (the foreign-securities line of reg. 15); fixed in regulation.\n")
in_block(MF, "MF-11", "(amends s.44 from 2.2.2027) · primary · checked 2026-10-25.",
         f"(amends s.44 from 2.2.2027) · primary · checked 2026-10-25. [חוק השקעות משותפות בנאמנות, התשנ\"ד-1994]({ISALAW}), p.37, s.46(ד) \"שר האוצר רשאי לקבוע בתקנות, דרך כלל או לסוגי קרנות, את היום שבו יעביר מפיץ את הסכום כאמור בסעיף 45\" · primary · checked 2026-10-26. [{PRICES_T}]({PRICES}), reg. 15(א)-(ב) \"בקרן שעל פי מדיניות ההשקעות שלה, לא יעלה שווי ניירות ערך חוץ שיוחזקו בה על עשרה אחוזים מהשווי הנקי של נכסיה\" · checked 2026-10-26 · primary (mirror). [קובץ התקנות 5637 (10.11.1994), סריקה באתר olaw]({K5637}), gazette p.326, reg. 15 as first enacted (read on the page image) · checked 2026-10-26 · primary (third-party host: olaw.org.il). [קובץ התקנות 5987 (1.7.1999), סריקה באתר olaw]({K5987}), gazette p.1026, s.12 (amends reg. 15(א)) (read on the page image) · checked 2026-10-26 · primary (third-party host: olaw.org.il). [{K11476_T}]({K11476}), gazette p.3700, rule 2(ב) \"בעל יחידות בקרן יוכל להגיש למפיץ הזמנות ליחידות או הוראות לפדיונן, במועדים הקבועים\"; in force 3.10.2024 (rule 6, p.7) · checked 2026-10-26 · primary (third-party host: olaw.org.il). [מזרחי טפחות: מידע נוסף על מתן הוראות בקרנות כספיות למועדים קבועים]({MIZ}) · checked 2026-10-26 · institution.")

oq_replace(MF, 4, "4. ~~When redemption cash is available to the holder in practice (same day as the price, or the next business day).~~ Closed 2026-10-26 (open-question hunt): reg. 15 of the prices regulations (1994, amended 1999) sets the day: in a fund whose investment policy keeps foreign securities at no more than 10% of net assets, the day the distributor must pass the order to the clearing house; otherwise the next trading day; a fixed-date fund executes orders only on its fixed date (ISA rules 2024, rule 2(ב)). Mizrahi Tefahot's next-business-day statement for fixed-date funds is that bank's own (MF-11).")

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- MF-10, MF-14 (MF OQ3)
in_block(MF, "MF-10", "The actual hours in force were not found (open question 3).",
         "For renewable money-market funds the bank must show the next date and hour for orders, and orders must be given \"עד לשעה היעודה בתאריך המוצג\" (directive 447A, appendix A, note 2); the Securities Authority's 2025 report shows 16:00 on the fixed date in its example of that display (an example, not the rule). A fixed-date fund's prospectus must state \"המועדים שבהם ניתן להגיש למפיץ הזמנות ליחידות הקרן והוראות לפדיונן, והמועד שבו הזמנות או הוראות כאמור יבוצעו\" (ISA rules 2024, rule 3(ב)(1)). The hours in force for daily funds, and the clearing house's rules that set them, were not found (open question 3, narrowed 2026-10-26).")
in_block(MF, "MF-10", "pp.22, 27 · primary (dated; still linked by the ISA as its full guide) · checked 2026-10-25.",
         f"pp.22, 27 · primary (dated; still linked by the ISA as its full guide) · checked 2026-10-25. [הוראת ניהול בנקאי תקין 447A: פרסום מידע מרוכז על קרנות כספיות ומק\"מ (04/25)]({A447A}), p.4, appendix A, note 2 \"יש לתת את ההוראות עד לשעה היעודה בתאריך המוצג\" · checked 2026-10-26 · primary. [פעילות קרנות נאמנות בישראל 2025 (רשות ניירות ערך)]({ISAREP}), p.19 (example of the bank display) · checked 2026-10-26 · primary. [{K11476_T}]({K11476}), gazette p.3700, rule 3(ב)(1) \"המועדים שבהם ניתן להגיש למפיץ הזמנות ליחידות הקרן והוראות לפדיונן\" · checked 2026-10-26 · primary (third-party host: olaw.org.il).")

MF14_OLD_RULE = "- Rule: Open. The 2017 ISA guide says units can be ordered or redeemed on every trading day, Sunday to Thursday for most funds, Monday to Thursday for funds with a material share of assets traded abroad. Two later secondary reports say TASE trading moved to Monday to Friday from the week beginning 5 January 2026 (ISA decision approved by the Finance Minister; Friday 9:25 to 13:50). They conflict on Fridays: one (5 Aug 2025) says Friday includes creations and redemptions of mutual-fund units, with Friday clearing-house instructions executed and settled on Sunday; the other (4 Jan 2026) says there are no Friday creations or redemptions in tracking and active funds on foreign indices."
in_block(MF, "MF-14", "### MF-14 Trading days for fund orders (open)", "### MF-14 Pricing days for fund orders: TASE trading days, and Monday to Thursday for funds not limited in foreign securities")
in_block(MF, "MF-14", MF14_OLD_RULE,
         "- Rule: A manager sells and redeems units of an open fund \"רק בימים שלגביהם עליו לחשב את מחיר הקניה ומחיר המכירה של נכסי הקרן\" (law s.46(א)), and computes those prices for every trading day (\"לגבי כל יום מסחר, לתום המסחר באותו יום\", prices regulations, reg. 2(א)). The regulations define \"יום מסחר\" (reg. 1): for a fund limited in foreign securities (\"קרן מוגבלת בניירות ערך חוץ\"), a day on which TASE trades and representative rates are published or interbank trading takes place; for a fund not so limited, \"כל אחד מהימים שני עד חמישי בשבוע שמתקיים בו מסחר בבורסה בישראל\". Since TASE has no Sunday session from 5.1.2026 (BRK-29), no fund order is executed on a Sunday, and a fund not limited in foreign securities takes no Friday orders.")
in_block(MF, "MF-14", "- Conditions / exceptions: Do not compute anything from this rule until an official source (ISA, TASE clearing rules or a current prospectus) is read.",
         "- Conditions / exceptions: Whether Friday is a pricing day for a fund limited in foreign securities turns on whether representative rates are published or interbank trading takes place that Friday (not checked). The regulations are read in the Wikisource consolidated text (amendments listed to 2018); a later amendment, for example for the move to Monday-to-Friday trading, was not checked in Reshumot. Background only, not sources of the rule: the 2017 ISA guide (Sunday to Thursday for most funds, Monday to Thursday for funds with a material share of assets abroad) and two press reports on the move to Monday-to-Friday trading that conflict on Friday creations and redemptions (5 Aug 2025: Friday orders executed and settled on Sunday; 4 Jan 2026: no Friday creations or redemptions in funds on foreign indices). Rewritten 2026-10-26 (open-question hunt, open question 3 narrowed).")
in_block(MF, "MF-14", "- Source: [ISA investor guide (2017)]",
         f"- Source: [חוק השקעות משותפות בנאמנות, התשנ\"ד-1994]({ISALAW}), p.36, s.46(א) \"רק בימים שלגביהם עליו לחשב את מחיר הקניה ומחיר המכירה של נכסי הקרן\" · primary · checked 2026-10-26. [{PRICES_T}]({PRICES}), reg. 1, definition \"יום מסחר\"; reg. 2(א) \"כל אחד מהימים שני עד חמישי בשבוע שמתקיים בו מסחר בבורסה בישראל\" · checked 2026-10-26 · primary (mirror). [ISA investor guide (2017)]")
in_block(MF, "MF-14", "· checked 2026-10-22 · secondary\n- Dimensions: liquidity-lockup",
         "· checked 2026-10-22 · secondary\n- Scope: general\n- Dimensions: liquidity-lockup")
in_block(MF, "MF-14", "- Likely to change: yes, recently changed; open",
         "- Likely to change: yes, if the regulations or the clearing house's rules change with the trading week.")

oq_append(MF, 3, "**[2026-10-26 open-question hunt]** Narrowed: orders are executed only on the fund's pricing days (law s.46(א)), which the prices regulations define (reg. 1 \"יום מסחר\": TASE trading days with representative rates or interbank trading for a fund limited in foreign securities; Monday to Thursday trading days for the others), so no Sunday execution since 5.1.2026 (MF-14); for renewable funds the bank shows the next date and hour (447A, appendix A, note 2) and the prospectus states when orders are taken and executed (ISA rules 2024, rule 3(ב)(1)) (MF-10). Still unknown: the designated hours in force for daily funds and the clearing house's rules that set them (TASE's trading-hours page loads through apicontent.tase.co.il, which answers 403 to scripts; not worked around); whether Friday is a pricing day for a fund limited in foreign securities; any amendment of the prices regulations after 2018.")
oq_append(MF, 1, "**[2026-10-26 open-question hunt]** The ISA rules of 2024 were read in a copy of the gazette (קובץ התקנות 11476, gazette p.3700, olaw.org.il, third-party host): rule 2(ב) (orders in a fixed-date fund are executed on the fixed date) and rule 3(ב)(1) (the prospectus states when orders are taken and executed), in force 3.10.2024 (rule 6) (MF-10, MF-11). The directive's final text is still open.")
oq_append(MF, 10, "**[2026-10-26 open-question hunt]** Narrowed for non-bank members as a class: the regulators' joint report (June 2026, p.11, read in funder.co.il's copy) says most non-bank members hold a marketing licence, have no distribution agreements, charge buy and sell commissions on active and passive fund units instead of a distribution fee, and customarily waive custody for their clients (practice, not binding) (BRK-52, MF-27). Still unknown: each member's own lines, and whether every manager has distribution agreements with every bank.")
